cardinalityOfConjugacyClass(Partition) -- the size of the conjugacy classes of S_n
**********************************************************************************

  * Function: *note cardinalityOfConjugacyClass:
    cardinalityOfConjugacyClass_lpPartition_rp,
  * Usage: 
        cardinalityOfConjugacyClass p
  * Inputs:
      * p, an instance of the type *note Partition: (Macaulay2Doc)Partition,, a
        partition that indexes a conjugacy class of S_n
  * Outputs:
      * an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the size of the conjugacy class

Description
===========

The formula for this classes is obtained by the Orbit-Stabilizer lemma applied
for S_n with the action of conjugation.

For a partition $p$ this formula is $n!/(\prod_i (\lambda_i )!i^\lambda_i$,
where $\lambda_i$ denotes the number of parts in $p$ that are equal to $i$.

+----------------------------------------+
|i1 : p1 = new Partition from {3,2,1}    |
|                                        |
|o1 = Partition{3, 2, 1}                 |
|                                        |
|o1 : Partition                          |
+----------------------------------------+
|i2 : cardinalityOfConjugacyClass p1     |
|                                        |
|o2 = 120                                |
+----------------------------------------+
|i3 : p2 = new Partition from {1,1,1,1,1}|
|                                        |
|o3 = Partition{1, 1, 1, 1, 1}           |
|                                        |
|o3 : Partition                          |
+----------------------------------------+
|i4 : cardinalityOfConjugacyClass p2     |
|                                        |
|o4 = 1                                  |
+----------------------------------------+

