characterTable -- returns the character table of the symmetric group
********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        characterTable n
  * Inputs:
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the degree of the symmetric
        group
  * Outputs:
      * an instance of the type *note CharacterTable: CharacterTable,, the
        character table with the irreducible characters of $S_n$ indexed by
        partitions

Description
===========

This method construct the irreducible characters of $S_n$. The method works by
recursively calculating the character tables for the permutation modules of
$S_n$. Then applying Gram-Schimdt algorithm to this characters using the inner
product of characters we obtain the irreducible characters of $S_n$

See also
========

  * *note CharacterTable: CharacterTable, -- the class of character tables

Ways to use characterTable:
===========================

  * "characterTable(ZZ)"

