higherSpechtPolynomials -- a method that gives sets of higher Specht polynomials
********************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        higherSpechtPolynomial(S,R)
        higherSpechtPolynomial(S,standard,R)
        higherSpechtPolynomial(p,R)
        higherSpechtPolynomial(R)
  * Inputs:
      * S, an instance of the type *note YoungTableau: YoungTableau,, 
      * R, a *note polynomial ring: (Macaulay2Doc)PolynomialRing,, 
      * standard, an instance of the type *note TableauList: TableauList,, The
        list of standard tableaux of the same shape as S
      * p, an instance of the type *note Partition: (Macaulay2Doc)Partition,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note AsExpression: AsExpression, => ..., default value false, an
        optional argument that returns polynomials as expressions
      * *note Robust: Robust, => ..., default value false, an optional argument
        for specifying the algorithm for calculating higherSpechtPolynomials
  * Outputs:
      * a *note hash table: (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable,, a hash table with
        multiple levels depending on the input

Description
===========

This methods returns higher Specht polynomials sorted in hash tables depending
on the input received.

If the input is just a YoungTableau $S$ of shape $\lambda$ and a PolynomialRing
then it calculates the standard tableaux $ST(\lambda)$ and then stores all
polynomials $F_T^S$ such that $T \in ST(\lambda)$. The polynomials are stored
in a hash table with the filling of $T$ as the key.

The list $ST(\lambda)$ can be provided as an input. This is used to avoid
repeating this calculation when this method is called multiple times with the
same shape $\lambda$.

This set forms a basis for one of the copies of the Specht module $S^\lambda$.



+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x_0..x_3]                                                        |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = R                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : p = new Partition from {2,2}                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = Partition{2, 2}                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Partition                                                               |
