indexMonomial(YoungTableau,YoungTableau,PolynomialRing) -- a monomial that represents an index tableau
******************************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note indexMonomial:
    indexMonomial_lpYoungTableau_cmYoungTableau_cmPolynomialRing_rp,
  * Usage: 
        indexMonomial(S,T,R)
  * Inputs:
      * S, an instance of the type *note YoungTableau: YoungTableau,, 
      * T, an instance of the type *note YoungTableau: YoungTableau,, 
      * R, a *note polynomial ring: (Macaulay2Doc)PolynomialRing,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, 

Description
===========

The index monomial is used in the construction of higher Specht polynomials. To
calculate the index monomial first the index tableau of $S$, $i(S)$ is
calculated. Then the monomial is calculated as $x_T^{i(S)}$. This is a monomial
with the variables as they appear in T with the exponents that appear in
$i(S)$.



+-------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x_0..x_4]                |
|                                     |
|o1 = R                               |
|                                     |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                  |
+-------------------------------------+
|i2 : p = new Partition from {2,2,1}  |
|                                     |
|o2 = Partition{2, 2, 1}              |
|                                     |
|o2 : Partition                       |
+-------------------------------------+
|i3 : S  = youngTableau(p,{0,2,1,3,4})|
|                                     |
|o3 = | 0 2 |                         |
|     | 1 3 |                         |
|     | 4 |                           |
|                                     |
|o3 : YoungTableau                    |
+-------------------------------------+
|i4 : T  = youngTableau(p,{0,1,2,3,4})|
|                                     |
|o4 = | 0 1 |                         |
|     | 2 3 |                         |
|     | 4 |                           |
|                                     |
|o4 : YoungTableau                    |
+-------------------------------------+
|i5 : ind = indexTableau(S)           |
|                                     |
|o5 = | 0 1 |                         |
|     | 1 2 |                         |
|     | 3 |                           |
|                                     |
|o5 : YoungTableau                    |
+-------------------------------------+
|i6 : indexMonomial(S,T,R)            |
|                                     |
|          2 3                        |
|o6 = x x x x                         |
|      1 2 3 4                        |
|                                     |
|o6 : R                               |
+-------------------------------------+

