indexTableau(YoungTableau) -- the index tableau for a given tableau
*******************************************************************

  * Function: *note indexTableau: indexTableau_lpYoungTableau_rp,
  * Usage: 
        indexTableau(y)
  * Inputs:
      * y, an instance of the type *note YoungTableau: YoungTableau,, 
  * Outputs:
      * an instance of the type *note YoungTableau: YoungTableau,, the index
        tableau

Description
===========

The index tableau is a filling obtained by the original tableau using the
reading word. To every element in the reading word a number is given
recursively in the following way. f(0) = 0 and f(k+1) = f(k) if k+1 appear to
the right of k. Otherwise f(k+1)= f(k)+1.

Finally the entries in the original tableau are replaced by the values of the
function f.



+------------------------------------+
|i1 : p = new Partition from {3,2}   |
|                                    |
|o1 = Partition{3, 2}                |
|                                    |
|o1 : Partition                      |
+------------------------------------+
|i2 : y = youngTableau(p,{0,2,3,1,4})|
|                                    |
|o2 = | 0 2 3 |                      |
|     | 1 4 |                        |
|                                    |
|o2 : YoungTableau                   |
+------------------------------------+
|i3 : readingWord(y)                 |
|                                    |
|o3 = {1, 0, 4, 2, 3}                |
|                                    |
|o3 : List                           |
+------------------------------------+
|i4 : indexTableau(y)                |
|                                    |
|o4 = | 0 1 1 |                      |
|     | 1 2 |                        |
|                                    |
|o4 : YoungTableau                   |
+------------------------------------+

