matrixRepresentation -- the matrix representation of a permutation in the Specht Module
***************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        matrixRepresentation(perm,standard)
        matrixRepresentation(perm,parti)
        matrixRepresentation(standard)
        matrixRepresentation(parti)
  * Inputs:
      * perm, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a permutation
      * standard, an instance of the type *note TableauList: TableauList,, a
        list of standard tableaux of a given partition
      * parti, an instance of the type *note Partition:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Partition,, a partition
  * Outputs:
      * a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, the matrix representation of the
        given permutation in the Specht module index by the given partition
      * a *note hash table: (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable,, if no permutation is
        given then it calculates the representation for all the permutations in
        S_n

Description
===========

The matrix representation for a permutation is calculated by studying the
action of the permutation on the basis of standard polytabloids.

The permuted polytabloids are then written as a linear combination of standard
polytabloids using the straightening algorithm.

+--------------------------------------+
|i1 : p = new Partition from {2,1}     |
|                                      |
|o1 = Partition{2, 1}                  |
|                                      |
|o1 : Partition                        |
+--------------------------------------+
|i2 : l = {0,2,1}                      |
|                                      |
|o2 = {0, 2, 1}                        |
|                                      |
|o2 : List                             |
