permutePolynomial -- permutes a RingElement or a PolynomialExpression of RingElements
*************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        permutePolynomial(perm,f)
        permutePolynomial(perm,prod)
        permutePolynomial(perm,s)
        permutePolynomial(perm,pow)
        permutePolynomial(perm,minu)
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, a ring element
      * prod, a *note product expression: (Macaulay2Doc)Product,, a Product
        expression
      * s, a *note sum expression: (Macaulay2Doc)Sum,, a sum expression
      * pow, a *note power expression: (Macaulay2Doc)Power,, a power expression
      * minu, a *note minus expression: (Macaulay2Doc)Minus,, a minus
        expression
      * perm, a permutation
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, the result of
        applying perm to f
      * an *note expression: (Macaulay2Doc)Expression,, the result of applying
        f to the given expression

Description
===========

This method applies permutations to polynomial ring elements by permuting the
variables. Therefore the size of the permutation must be equal to the number of
generators of the ring of the elements.

+---------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x_0..x_4]      |
|                           |
|o1 = R                     |
|                           |
|o1 : PolynomialRing        |
+---------------------------+
|i2 : l = {1,0,2,3,4}       |
|                           |
|o2 = {1, 0, 2, 3, 4}       |
|                           |
|o2 : List                  |
+---------------------------+
|i3 : f = x_1*x_2*x_3       |
|                           |
|o3 = x x x                 |
|      1 2 3                |
|                           |
|o3 : R                     |
+---------------------------+
|i4 : permutePolynomial(l,f)|
|                           |
|o4 = x x x                 |
|      0 2 3                |
|                           |
|o4 : R                     |
+---------------------------+

This method can also permute polynomial expressions that are constructed from
ring elements either by sums, products or powers.

+-------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : ex = factor(x_1*x_2*x_3)+factor(x_1*x_3*x_4)|
|                                                 |
|o5 = (x )(x )(x ) + (x )(x )(x )                 |
|       3   2   1      4   3   1                  |
|                                                 |
|o5 : Expression of class Sum                     |
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : permutePolynomial(l,ex)                     |
|                                                 |
|o6 = (x )(x )(x ) + (x )(x )(x )                 |
|       3   2   0      4   3   0                  |
|                                                 |
|o6 : Expression of class Sum                     |
+-------------------------------------------------+

