rowPermutationTableaux(YoungTableau) -- the list of row permutations without repetitions in columns
***************************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note rowPermutationTableaux:
    rowPermutationTableaux_lpYoungTableau_rp,
  * Usage: 
        rowPermutationTableaux(y)
  * Inputs:
      * y, an instance of the type *note YoungTableau: YoungTableau,, a
        tableau, generally the index tableau of a standard tableau
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, the list of all row permutations of
        the tableau

Description
===========

This list of tableaux is used to calculate more efficiently higher Specht
polynomials. If any of the columns has a repetition then the associated term in
the higher Specht polynomial for this row permutation is zero. This is why such
permutations are omitted.



+--------------------------------------+
|i1 : p = new Partition from {3,2}     |
|                                      |
|o1 = Partition{3, 2}                  |
|                                      |
|o1 : Partition                        |
+--------------------------------------+
|i2 : y = youngTableau(p, {0,2,1,3,4}) |
|                                      |
|o2 = | 0 2 1 |                        |
|     | 3 4 |                          |
|                                      |
|o2 : YoungTableau                     |
+--------------------------------------+
|i3 : ind = indexTableau y             |
|                                      |
|o3 = | 0 1 0 |                        |
|     | 2 2 |                          |
|                                      |
|o3 : YoungTableau                     |
+--------------------------------------+
|i4 : rowPermutationTableaux ind       |
|                                      |
|o4 = {| 0 0 1 |, | 0 1 0 |, | 1 0 0 |}|
|      | 2 2 |    | 2 2 |    | 2 2 |   |
|                                      |
|o4 : List                             |
+--------------------------------------+

