spechtPolynomial(YoungTableau,PolynomialRing) -- the Specht polynomial indexed by a standard tableau
****************************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note spechtPolynomial:
    spechtPolynomial_lpYoungTableau_cmPolynomialRing_rp,
  * Usage: 
        spechtPolynomial(y,R)
  * Inputs:
      * y, an instance of the type *note YoungTableau: YoungTableau,, 
      * R, a *note polynomial ring: (Macaulay2Doc)PolynomialRing,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note AsExpression: AsExpression, => ..., default value false, an
        optional argument that returns polynomials as expressions
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, the Specht polynomial

Description
===========

Specht polynomials were the original objects that gave rise to the Specht
modules. The Specht polynomial of a tableau $T$ is product of the Vandermonde
determinant of the variables index by the columns of the tableau.



+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x_0..x_4]                                                        |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = R                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : p = new Partition from {2,2,1}                                          |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = Partition{2, 2, 1}                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Partition                                                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : y = youngTableau(p,{0,3,1,4,2})                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = | 0 3 |                                                                 |
|     | 1 4 |                                                                 |
|     | 2 |                                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : YoungTableau                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : spechtPolynomial(y,R)                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|      2          2      2        2          2        2      2          2     |
|o4 = x x x  - x x x  - x x x  + x x x  + x x x  - x x x  - x x x  + x x x  + |
|      0 1 3    0 1 3    0 2 3    1 2 3    0 2 3    1 2 3    0 1 4    0 1 4   |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|      2        2          2        2                                         |
|     x x x  - x x x  - x x x  + x x x                                        |
|      0 2 4    1 2 4    0 2 4    1 2 4                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : R                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : factor oo                                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = (x  - x )(x  - x )(x  - x )(x  - x )                                    |
|       3    4   1    2   0    2   0    1                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : Expression of class Product                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

