straighteningAlgorithm -- an algorithm for expressing any polytabloid as linear combinations of standard polytabloids
*********************************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        straighteningAlgorithm(ele)
        straighteningAlgorithm(y,coef)
        straighteningAlgorithm(y)
  * Inputs:
      * ele, an instance of the type *note SpechtModuleElement:
        SpechtModuleElement,, a SpecthModuleElement
      * y, an instance of the type *note YoungTableau: YoungTableau,, a tableau
        that labels a polytabloid
      * coef, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the coefficient of the
        polytabloid
  * Outputs:
      * an instance of the type *note SpechtModuleElement:
        SpechtModuleElement,, the same SpechtModuleElement written as a linear
        combination of standard polytabloids

Description
===========

The straigtening algorithm works by finding the first term that is not
standard. Then, taking as coordinates the first row descent, it calculates the
Garnir element of this tableaux. It then rewrites the SpechtModuleElement
substituting the term by the linear combination given by the garnir element.

+----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : p = new Partition from {3,2,1}                                         |
|                                                                            |
|o1 = Partition{3, 2, 1}                                                     |
|                                                                            |
|o1 : Partition                                                              |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : y = youngTableau(p,{1,2,3,5,4,6})                                      |
|                                                                            |
|o2 = | 1 2 3 |                                                              |
|     | 5 4 |                                                                |
|     | 6 |                                                                  |
|                                                                            |
|o2 : YoungTableau                                                           |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : garnirElement y                                                        |
|                                                                            |
|o3 = - | 1 2 3 | + | 1 2 3 | + | 1 4 3 | - | 1 4 3 | + | 1 5 3 | + | 1 2 3 ||
|       | 4 5 |     | 4 6 |     | 2 5 |     | 2 6 |     | 2 6 |     | 5 4 |  |
|       | 6 |       | 5 |       | 6 |       | 5 |       | 4 |       | 6 |    |
|                                                                            |
|o3 : SpechtModuleElement                                                    |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

